WEBVTT

NOTE
Interlock — RC1 narration and caption track.
Cues are derived from the measured narration, not authored alongside it.
Technical tokens are printed exactly as the system emits them; the spoken
form is the natural-language reading of the same token.

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.583
Two autonomous agents can each be right, and
still be wrong together.

2
00:00:07.083 --> 00:00:11.900
Together they break a constraint that spans
both targets.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:18.773
The lock sees one key, and it is right about
that key.

4
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:27.635
The hazard crossed two keys. No single key
represents the pair.

5
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:33.587
Interlock isn't another agent. It's the
deterministic boundary

6
00:00:33.587 --> 00:00:38.223
those actions pass through before shared state
changes.

7
00:00:38.723 --> 00:00:45.921
Revision-bound evidence about the environment
enters that boundary before anything mutates.

8
00:00:46.471 --> 00:00:51.371
Four coordination strategies, one frozen
corpus.

9
00:00:51.871 --> 00:00:55.625
Global serialization avoided the invalid
outcomes

10
00:00:55.625 --> 00:00:59.642
— by making the independent work wait too.

11
00:01:00.142 --> 00:01:06.590
The per-target lock kept that work parallel,
and missed both hazards.

12
00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:11.865
Now hold everything constant except the
evidence.

13
00:01:12.365 --> 00:01:17.952
With the coupling evidence present, the
hazardous compositions were withheld.

14
00:01:18.452 --> 00:01:28.114
Remove it, and the decision flips to
ALLOW_PARALLEL. The invalid outcomes return.

15
00:01:29.214 --> 00:01:31.387
That's the controlled evaluation.

16
00:01:31.887 --> 00:01:36.047
Separately, here's the system running on
Google Cloud.

17
00:01:38.547 --> 00:01:44.407
The deployed Cloud Run agent, reading back its
own configuration:

18
00:01:44.407 --> 00:01:49.704
gemini-3.5-flash, through Google ADK, on
Vertex AI.

19
00:01:50.204 --> 00:01:57.547
Three Cloud Run services carry it: the agent,
the Interlock proxy, and the protected target.

20
00:01:58.047 --> 00:02:03.061
Now one run, start to finish, without a cut.

21
00:02:08.547 --> 00:02:11.047
Interlock returns ALLOW, with a receipt.

22
00:02:11.547 --> 00:02:17.552
The mutation is EXECUTED, a separately
authenticated observer OBSERVED it,

23
00:02:17.552 --> 00:02:21.947
and Cloud Logging carries the same run id.

24
00:02:22.497 --> 00:02:24.940
Identity answers who called.

25
00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:28.341
Interlock answers a different question:

26
00:02:28.341 --> 00:02:33.436
whether these two actions may proceed
together.

27
00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:37.118
Three fail-closed controls were recorded on
that run.

28
00:02:37.618 --> 00:02:44.764
Three controls are three controls — not
comprehensive security coverage.

29
00:02:45.314 --> 00:02:48.584
Sixteen frozen scenarios, enumerated
exhaustively.

30
00:02:49.084 --> 00:02:53.913
Exact counts. No interval, and no
significance, is claimed.

31
00:02:54.463 --> 00:02:59.049
Two runs, two proof classes. Neither is
evidence for the other.

32
00:02:59.549 --> 00:03:07.169
No exactly-once execution, no restart safety,
no production readiness.

33
00:03:07.719 --> 00:03:10.822
If your effects and invariants all fit inside

34
00:03:10.822 --> 00:03:14.932
one transactional authority, enforce them
there.

35
00:03:15.432 --> 00:03:21.546
Interlock explores the harder boundary:
independently proposed actions,

36
00:03:21.546 --> 00:03:28.285
different targets, coupled through shared
environmental state.

37
00:03:28.835 --> 00:03:35.238
Interlock. Evidence-bound coordination for
AI-assisted change.
